<!-- Part 14 e2e scenario: a THIRD contradiction axis, orthogonal to both
     test_vt_contradiction.NodeSet2 (an instance declaration's ValueRank vs.
     the SAME BrowseName's own ancestor-declaration, across the ObjectType
     hierarchy) and test_vt_datatype_contradiction.NodeSet2 (DataType, same
     axis as the ValueRank one). Here the conflict is between a
     VariableType's OWN declared ValueRank (an attribute of the type
     itself, not of any instance) and an *instance declaration's own
     explicit ValueRank override*, where the instance's TypeDefinition IS
     that exact VariableType.

     VariableSubType <: BaseDataVariableType (real, i=63): declares its OWN
     ValueRank=1 (OneDimension) directly on the type, not on any instance.
     BType: Mandatory "Var2" : BaseDataVariableType, instance-level
     ValueRank=-1 (Scalar) explicit.
     BSubType <: BType: redeclares "Var2", retyped to VariableSubType, still
     with instance-level ValueRank=-1 (Scalar) explicit, unchanged from
     BType's own declaration, but now incompatible with its new nominal
     type's own OneDimension rank.

     Before _add_own_variable_type_restrictions existed, a VariableType's
     own ValueRank/DataType were never modeled as OWL axioms at all (only
     an *instance declaration's* ValueRank/DataType were), so
     VariableSubType carried no ValueRank relationship whatsoever, and this
     scenario was NOT caught: VT(BSubType,"Var2") was subClassOf
     VariableSubType and had its own hasValueRank someValuesFrom/
     allValuesFrom ValueRank_Scalar (its own instance-level rank), but
     VariableSubType itself asserted nothing for a reasoner to conflict
     with. Now VariableSubType also carries hasValueRank someValuesFrom/
     allValuesFrom ValueRank_OneDimension (its own explicit rank); since
     hasValueRank is Functional, VT(BSubType,"Var2")'s single permitted
     value would have to be simultaneously Scalar (its own) and
     OneDimension (inherited via VariableSubType): disjoint, unsatisfiable,
     confirmed by real HermiT. -->
